\[ q(f_1 F^1) = \{ e_1\} = p(\mathcal F^1_{f_1}) = p(\mathcal F^1_{f_2}); \quad q(f_2F^1) = \{ e_2\} = p(\mathcal F^1_{f_3}); \text{ and} \quad q(f_3 F^1) = \{ e_3\} = p(\mathcal F^2_{f_3}).\]
As $p(f_1) = p(f_2) = v$ and $q(f_3) = w,$ we have 
\[ \mathcal E^1_{v} = p(\mathcal F^1_{f_1}) = \{e_1\} = p(\mathcal F^1_{f_2}), \qquad  \mathcal E^1_{w} = p(\mathcal F^1_{f_3}) = \{e_2\}, \quad \text{ and } \quad \mathcal E^2_w = \{ e_3\}.\]
It follows that 

