\end{equation}
}
where $u_{\xi},v_{\xi},w_{\xi}$ can have complex entries because they represent Fourier-transformed velocity components. $N_y$ is the number of points that are used in the discretization of the wall-normal direction. \red{Eq. \eqref{eq:delta_u} represents the structure that arises after a discretization of Eq. \eqref{eq:u_xi}}. \red{This structure insures} that the feedback interconnection loop in Fig.~\ref{fig:block_diagram} \red{accurately recreate the structure of the nonlinear advection term}.
