\section{\red{Derivation of bound on perturbation magnitude}}
\label{sec:App_theory}

\red{
Here, we explicitly derive an expression for the norm $\norm{\mathbf{u}_{\Xi}}_{\infty}$, to show that it is equivalent to the largest perturbation magnitude in the flow, as stated in~\S\ref{subsec: small gain}.

Based on Eq.~\ref{eq:u_xi}, the explicit expression for $\mathbf{u}_{\Xi}$ is:
%%
\begin{equation}
    \label{eq:u_xi_app}
    \mathbf{u}_{\Xi} = 
    \begin{bmatrix}
        -u(y) & -v(y) & -w(y) & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\
        0 & 0 & 0 & -u(y) & -v(y) & -w(y) & 0 & 0 & 0 \\
        0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -u(y) & -v(y) & -w(y)
    \end{bmatrix}.
\end{equation}
%%
Using the definition in Eq.~\ref{eq:u_xi_app}, we obtain
%%
\begin{equation}
    \label{eq:u_xi*}
    \mathbf{u}_{\Xi}^* = 
    \begin{bmatrix}
        -u^*(y) & 0 & 0 \\
        -v^*(y) & 0 & 0 \\
        -w^*(y) & 0 & 0 \\
        0 & -u^*(y) & 0 \\
        0 & -v^*(y) & 0 \\
        0 & -w^*(y) & 0 \\
        0 & 0 & -u^*(y) \\
        0 & 0 & -v^*(y) \\
        0 & 0 & -w^*(y)
    \end{bmatrix}.
\end{equation}
%%
We multiply the results of Eq.~\ref{eq:u_xi_app} and Eq.~\ref{eq:u_xi*} to obtain the following result
\begin{equation}
    \label{eq:u*u}
    \mathbf{u}_{\Xi}\mathbf{u}_{\Xi}^* = \left[ |u(y)|^2 + |v(y)|^2 + |w(y)|^2\right] I_{3\times 3},
\end{equation}
%%
where $I_{3\times 3}$ is a $3$-by-$3$ identity matrix. 

By definition of the singular value:
%%
\begin{equation}
    \label{eq:SV_def}
    \bar{\sigma}(\mathbf{u}_{\Xi}) = \sqrt{\bar{\lambda}(\mathbf{u}_{\Xi}\mathbf{u}_{\Xi}^*)}.
\end{equation}
%%
Here, $\bar{\lambda}(\cdot)$ represents the largest eigenvalue of a matrix. Since all eigenvalues of an identity matrix are equal to $1$, using Eq.~\ref{eq:u*u} and Eq.~\ref{eq:SV_def} it is clear that the following is true
%%
\begin{equation}
    \label{eq:sigma_u*u}
        \bar{\sigma}(\mathbf{u}_{\Xi}) = \sqrt{|u(y)|^2 + |v(y)|^2 + |w(y)|^2} = \norm{\mathbf{u}(y)}_2.
\end{equation}
%%
By the definition of the $\mathscr{H}_\infty$ norm and the result of Eq.~\ref{eq:sigma_u*u}, we obtain the following result:
\begin{equation}
    \label{H_inf_norm_app}
    \norm{\mathbf{u}_{\Xi}}_{\infty} = \sup_{y\in \mathcal{Y}} \bar{\sigma}(\mathbf{u}_{\Xi}) = \sup_{y\in \mathcal{Y}} \norm{\mathbf{u}(y)}_2.
\end{equation}
%%
This proves the result stated in Eq.~\ref{eq: barsig} and shows that a bound on the norm of the uncertainty matrix $\mathbf{u}_{\Xi}$ is equivalent to a bound on the magnitude of perturbations in the flow.
}


