    \caption{Power spectrum of the difference between LPT and EPT fields at~$z=0.5$ in linear and cubic models, normalized by~$P_{
    \rm PT}$, see Eq.~\eqref{eq:Perr_DM}. The shaded region corresponds to a relative error smaller than~$5\%$. Note that~$P_{\rm err.}/P_{\rm PT}\approx 2 \Delta A/ A$. Thin vertical line marks the maximum wavenumber used in the analysis,~$k_{\rm max}=0.12\;h/{\rm Mpc}$. At higher redshifts the agreement between EPT and LPT is even better.}
    \label{fig:cross_coeff_mat_err}
