\caption{Steady-state optimised subgraph of the H-P flows for the triangular configuration obtained with the \textbf{Random pair} and \textbf{Random random} algorithms. The best communication network is the one with the smallest $\nu$. We also depict the graph $\mathcal{G}$ obtained as the Delaunay triangulation of the point lattice on the unit square. The steady-state subgraphs follow the edges of the fixed graph $\mathcal{G}$, and their width is proportional to the adapted channel radius. In the limit $N \to \infty$, the edges connecting the sources and sinks converge to straight lines.}
\label{fig:tri_random}
