\section{Conclusion} \label{sec:conclusion}
We propose \texttt{LighthouseGS}, a practical 3DGS-based novel view synthesis framework for indoor scenes from panorama-style motion capture with a single mobile device.
%
To address the inherent challenges of motion and indoor scenes, we leverage planar structures throughout the entire pipeline.
%
Specifically, we newly introduce a planar scaffold assembly that aligns 3D points to ensure global and local consistency, initializing 3D Gaussians to fit the scene geometry accurately.
%
In addition, we propose a novel plane-aware stable optimization, which retains highly confident Gaussians in non-textured regions.
%
We further correct inaccurate camera poses and auto-exposure images to enhance visual quality.
%
Experiments demonstrate that \texttt{LighthouseGS} achieves photorealistic rendering while preserving precise scene geometry, expanding its versatility for general users in a wide range of applications.
