\section{Conclusions}

This paper considered a multiplet of two spin $\frac{1}{2}$ particles 
with equal (or almost equal mass). It demonstrated that for a Lorentz 
invariant equation describing this multiplet there exists a kinematical 
gauge of three types. The rest of the paper explored briefly    
the possible impact of this gauge on the interaction of this multiplet
with an external electromagnetic field and its motion
in central force field.


