\subsection{Zigzag Depth Paradox}
\label{sec:gallery-zigzag}
%------------------------------------------

A distinct class of visual paradoxes emerges when we consider depth ambiguity rather than height differentiation. Consider the zigzag path constructed of segments which alternates direction at each corner in Figure \ref{fig:zigzag}[top]. When extended infinitely on each side or wrapped around a cylinder there is no paradox.

