During the temporal delay between these snapshots, the initially coherent upstream traveling beam undergoes a transition to a diffuse population, a process that correlates with the saturation of wave growth.
In parallel, the core species of the inflow are subject to subtle modulations resulting from the ULF wave perturbations.


