\begin{abstract}
\noindent

In this paper, by selecting appropriate spectral matrices within the loop algebra of symplectic Lie algebra $\mathfrak{sp}(6)$, we construct two distinct classes of integrable soliton hierarchies. Then, by employing the Tu scheme and trace identity, we derive the Hamiltonian structures of the aforementioned two classes of integrable systems. From these two classes of integrable soliton hierarchies, we select one particular hierarchy and employ the Kronecker product to construct an integrable coupling system.
\end{abstract}
