	Let~\(P := G \bx H\). We first introduce two types of edges in~\(P\). Then, we show that these edge sets are preserved under automorphisms of~\(P\). Using that there are two Hamiltonian cycles of~\(P\) containing a different number of edges from each of the respective two edge sets, we can then deduce that~\(P \not \in \mH\).

