	Let $k:=|G|$, $l:=|H|$ and fix a Hamiltonian cycle of $G$ and of $H$.
	Using these, we can construct the Hamiltonian cycle of~\(P\) depicted on the left of Figure~\ref{fig:can-ham-cyc-cart-prod}. (Note that the construction slightly changes depending on the parity of \(|H|\), but the following arguments hold for both.) This cycle has~\(2(l-1)\) edges in~\(E_H\) and~\(2(k-1)+(l-2)(k-2)\) edges in~\(E_G\).

