		and consider the associated T-RAAG Lie algebra over $k$.

		Let $y'=y_1+y_2$. One has $[y',x]=[y_1,x]+[y_2,x]=2x\2=0$. It follows that the assignment $\phi(x)=x'$, $\phi(y_1)=y_1'$, $\phi(y_2)=y_1'+y'$ defines an isomorphism between $\mf a(\Gamma)$ and the restricted Lie algebra \[\pres{x',y'_1,y'}{[x',y'],[x',y_1']={x'}\2}\]
		which means that the graph  \[\Gamma'=\begin{tikzpicture}
			\node[fill=black!100,circle,scale=0.3,draw,"$x$"] at (0,-1) {};
