		For RACG, the BK property is not equivalent to the fact that all standard subalgebras are RACG. For instance, if $\Gamma$ is discrete with two vertices, then the subalgebra generated by the sum of the canonical generators is not elementary abelian, as it should be if it were a RACG (on a singleton graph). 
